#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0131 expect=noViolation domain=ADLB
#note "PLAN-function-surface-wave1 phase 4: a group whose PARAMCD key is MISSING. The rule declares Grouping: Variables: [PARAMCD] (Sensitivity Group), and the RULE-LEVEL grouping defaults to DROP_MISSING_KEYS (RuleRunner, GroupKeyPolicy.DROP_MISSING_KEYS.withDeclared(rule.groupingKeepMissings())), so the two missing-PARAMCD rows are dropped before any finding is reported, whatever has_mixed_emptiness_within_group answers for them (its own default KEEP_MISSING_KEYS folds them into one mixed group, pinned by the engine's unit matrix). Measured at the wave's go on the pre-port engine: no finding; the port preserves it. ALB is consistent. A finding here would mean the rule-level drop stopped applying."
#library standard=adamig version=1-2
dataset ADLB
col USUBJID  type=Char
col PARAMCD  type=Char
col BASETYPE type=Char
---
S1 |     | X
S2 |     |
S3 | ALB | Y
S4 | ALB | Y
